course: dictionary
lesson: 7149
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Perch can be a noun or a verb. «Mr Crow, perched in a tree, held a cheese in his beak.» Here the clues are tree and beak, so perched means sat up high on a branch.
explain: Check the clues around the word. In «The harpy eagle perches on emergent trees», the eagle is a bird, so perches means sits on something high. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "The harpy eagle sits on emergent trees" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Perch can also mean to put something in a high or wobbly place, as in «Toad's rusty black bonnet was perched over one eye.» The bonnet is not sitting, it is balanced on top of his head. Context tells you what kind of perching is happening.
explain: When a word is also a noun for a thing, like a fish, look for words such as lakes, rivers or catch. «Anglers catch perch in lakes and rivers.» Here perch is a fish. If the clues do not fit, the dictionary will settle it.
fact: A perch is a branch, bar or stick where a bird sits.
fact: To perch means to sit on something high or narrow, the way a bird does.
fact: To perch something means to put it in a high or wobbly place.
fact: A perch is also a freshwater fish with spiny fins that people catch and eat.
fact: Perching birds, such as sparrows, have feet that grip branches, and pet budgies have a perch in their cage.
exercise: «Mr Crow, perched in a tree, held a cheese in his beak.» What does perched mean here? | Swam in a lake | Hid under a rock | Dropped to the ground | *Sat up high on a branch
exercise: «Anglers catch perch in lakes and rivers.» What kind of perch is this? | A high, narrow shelf | A bird's branch | A place to sit at a table | *A freshwater fish with spiny fins
exercise: «Toad's rusty black bonnet was perched over one eye.» What does perched suggest about the bonnet? | *Balanced in a high, wobbly spot | Washed clean and folded | Pulled tight and sewn on | Thrown on the floor
test: «The harpy eagle perches on emergent trees and swoops into the canopy.» Which word tells you the eagle is sitting high? | Swoops | Canopy | *Perches | Emergent
test: Mia says perch always means a fish. Which sentence is the best reply? | *No, perch can mean a branch where a bird sits, or to sit high on something | Yes, perch is always a fish | Perch means to swim quickly | No, perch is always a bird
exam: «Pet budgies have a perch in their cage.» In this sentence, what is a perch? | *A branch, bar or stick where a bird sits | A fish that lives in the cage | To sit on something high | A high, narrow shelf for books
